            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted complete lecture notes, Chapter 6, §§6.2.1–6.2.2",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html"
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 complete prepublication book draft, §§54–56",
              "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "Roy J. Glauber, “Coherent and Incoherent States of the Radiation Field,” Physical Review 131 (1963), 2766–2788, §§II–III and IX",
              "url": "https://www.ifi.unicamp.br/~cabrera/teaching/aula%2016%202011s1.pdf"
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 8,
        "physical_scope": "Fixed finite massive prescribed charge-flow current, measurable transverse polarizations, and finite photon-energy cutoffs 0 < lambda < Lambda. The result is the exact count distribution and mean energy of the constructed normalized positive-free-photon coherent state under the adopted finite projective Born interpretation. For positive angular coefficient the zero-cutoff family has no Fock-vector or projective-ray limit despite bounded mean energy. No interacting-QED scattering event, detector response, or empirical observation is asserted.",
        "empirical_premises": []
      }
    ]
